(vector
 (map
  (:adr/id "adr-2609112700-a-refusal-scoped-wider-than-its-reason")
  (:adr/title "A refusal scoped wider than its reason")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2609112500-a-hash-that-does-not-vary-with-the-repository"))
  (:adr/body "
## What was frozen

com-aftership, com-adyen and com-airtable declare :refs {} on every spec.
The generator refused the whole run on that basis, so each improvement
since -- the entity table, the fixtures, oracle-filters, oracle-handlers,
none of which touch a ref -- stopped at that one line.

Measured 2026-09-11, all three still carried both defects already fixed
everywhere else: oracle-filters answering the same number for all six
selectors, and handler selector 6 measuring 400 with selector 13 hashing
an absent field.

That is the compounding shape. A refusal scoped wider than its reason does
not just block one thing once; it blocks everything afterwards, quietly,
and the gap grows with every fix that lands elsewhere.

## What was NOT relaxed

The reasoning behind the refusal is intact. A generator that invented a
ref pair would manufacture the input whose absence it exists to detect,
and its arms would go green over a fold the production path never
performs. Nothing here invents one.

## Skipping did not work, and the floor said so

The first attempt skipped the ref blocks and regenerated the rest. The
evidence floor refused: the generator builds from the TEMPLATE, so an
un-regenerated cred-row keeps parentPartId, childPartId and the BOM
entity, and the output would name a relationship the repository does not
have.

I had checked the SHIPPED components for those tokens and found none, and
concluded skipping was safe. The generator does not start from the shipped
component. The floor caught the error that reading had not.

## So the blocks are deleted

cred-row, seeded-both and oracle-expand form a closed cluster: cred-row
feeds seeded-both, both feed oracle-expand, and the only tie outside it is
the oracle-expand export. The three come out together, and the export with
them.

That is a public-surface change, of the kind ADR-q9 allows by explicit API
decision. It is the right one: a fold over nothing should be absent rather
than present and vacuous, which is the same rule the harness already
states for its own arms.

## Two things the refusal had been hiding

The substitution table resolves ref-prefix and ref-ent through the ref
entity, which is nil here. str/replace with a nil replacement throws from
inside clojure.string, naming the reducer rather than the token -- an
error that says where it broke and not what broke. Substituting a token
for nothing is never right, so a nil replacement is now dropped and
REPORTED.

That report earned itself immediately. It names BOM, which survives in
oracle-store's last selector: in these three repositories that selector
queries an entity the repository does not have. It still returns 0, so the
store-layer parity landed earlier measured five of five agreeing -- the
harness queries a real other entity holding no rows, the component queries
a nonexistent one, and both answer 0. Agreement for two different reasons.
Recorded here; not fixed in this iteration.

## Reproduce

    kbb --backend sci scripts/gen-whole-component.cljk <template> <worktree> <src-dir>

A ref-less repository now prints DROPPED-BLOCKS and SKIPPED-TOKENS and
writes; a ref-having one prints neither and is byte-for-byte idempotent.

    filters  before 5,5,5,5,5,5   after 5,5,0,1,0,5
    handlers before sel6=400 sel13=7   after sel6=200 sel13=<hash>

com-airtable is 5,5,0,5,5,5: Base declares :fields and :required
identical, so no field carries a row index and the two uniqueness
selectors are omitted with a comment rather than faked by repeating a
required field. The floor -- selector 1 matches every row, selector 2 none
-- is met.

## Control

On a ref-having repository the patched generator is byte-for-byte
idempotent and prints neither new line. Without that control the change
could have altered seventeen components silently.

## Still outside

com-airbus-analytx remains skipped for a different and unchanged reason:
it is hand adapted, 16 added and 23 removed lines against the generator's
output, and is not machine rewritten.

com-abb-robotics, the template itself, is still not a fixed point of its
own generator.
")))
